  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Everyone carries one or two given names and two family names: the father's first family name, then the mother's first family name (María García López). Since 2017 parents may choose the order. Women keep their own family names when they marry. In everyday life people go by the first family name, or by both when the first is very common. Compound given names are common (José Luis, María José, Juan Carlos) and get shortened (Josele, Mariajo). In Catalonia, the Basque Country and Galicia many people carry names in their own language (Jordi, Núria, Iker, Ane) and Catalan family names are joined with i (Puig i Ferrer). Spain's cities also have large Latin American, Moroccan, Romanian, Chinese and Pakistani communities.",
